{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceWeightsOfAlgEquiv","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TraceWeightsOfAlgEquiv","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceIsWeighted"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.exists_ne_zero_forall_mul_eq_zero_of_traceWeight_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.exists_ne_zero_forall_mul_eq_zero_of_traceWeight_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceWeightsOfAlgEquiv.lean#L73-L101","doc":"**A vanishing block weight puts a whole block in the radical.**\n\nIf `c_i = 0` then the pullback of the diagonal unit `E^{(i)}_{aa}` is a\nnonzero element `z` with `t (z y) = 0` for *every* `y` — so the form\n`(x, y) ↦ t(x y)` is degenerate.  Contrapositive: a nondegenerate `t` has\nevery weight nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.eq_weightedTrace_of_algEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.eq_weightedTrace_of_algEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceWeightsOfAlgEquiv.lean#L66-L71","doc":"**A trace on a split algebra is a weighted trace, through the splitting.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.traceWeight_indep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.traceWeight_indep","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceWeightsOfAlgEquiv.lean#L60-L64","doc":"**The weight does not depend on which diagonal unit is used.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.comp_symm_mul_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.comp_symm_mul_comm","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceWeightsOfAlgEquiv.lean#L51-L57","doc":"The composite `t ∘ E.symm` is a trace on the product whenever `t` is one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.traceWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.traceWeight","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceWeightsOfAlgEquiv.lean#L44-L48","doc":"**The weight of block `i`**: the value of `t` on the pullback of a diagonal\nmatrix unit.  Well defined independently of the unit — `traceWeight_indep`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}